WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.856 --> 00:00:02.975
- When my little brother Lucas was born,

00:00:02.975 --> 00:00:05.231
my parents were told that
he wouldn't walk or talk

00:00:05.231 --> 00:00:07.514
and the doctors even
said he might not make it

00:00:07.514 --> 00:00:09.347
to his tenth birthday.

00:00:10.436 --> 00:00:12.809
But today, a few months away
from his tenth birthday,

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:16.559
we're doing our fifteenth
triathlon together.

00:00:21.911 --> 00:00:23.004
My name is Noah Aldrich,

00:00:23.004 --> 00:00:24.986
and this is my brother, Lucas Aldrich.

00:00:24.986 --> 00:00:26.708
- (vocalizing)

00:00:26.708 --> 00:00:29.625
- Lucas, you've gotta stop talking.

00:00:30.954 --> 00:00:32.122
Gotta get the guy, Luke.

00:00:32.122 --> 00:00:35.051
- Noah is 11, and Lucas is nine,

00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:37.543
and Lucas was born with
a rare genetic neurologic

00:00:37.543 --> 00:00:40.559
condition called lissencephaly.

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:43.001
He's unable to walk, unable to talk,

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:44.701
he's unable to feed himself,

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.345
but despite all of his challenges,

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:50.512
he's the happiest little
boy that you'll ever meet.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:55.035
- About four years ago,
our boys started doing

00:00:55.035 --> 00:00:57.476
triathlons together, and most cases

00:00:57.476 --> 00:00:59.853
that wouldn't be a big deal,
a lot of kids do triathlons,

00:00:59.853 --> 00:01:03.097
but there's something
very special about the way

00:01:03.097 --> 00:01:05.014
our boys do triathlons.

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:11.410
- I pull Lucas in a raft
for the swim portion.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:15.595
Then, I pull him in a bike
cart during the bike.

00:01:15.595 --> 00:01:19.595
And I push him in a running
cart during the run.

00:01:21.122 --> 00:01:22.806
I wanted to do this because
Lucas can't do things

00:01:22.806 --> 00:01:23.806
like we can.

00:01:24.758 --> 00:01:26.595
He can't really play sports,

00:01:26.595 --> 00:01:29.645
so this is something we can do together.

00:01:29.645 --> 00:01:32.610
Currently, we're training
for our fifteenth triathlon,

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.949
which is this weekend.

00:01:34.949 --> 00:01:36.792
Before the race I always feel nervous.

00:01:36.792 --> 00:01:38.638
I don't think I'll ever get over that.

00:01:38.638 --> 00:01:40.604
I just don't want to hurt Lucas.

00:01:40.604 --> 00:01:42.001
I don't care if I win the race,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.918
he just has to be okay.

00:01:48.716 --> 00:01:50.778
- [Alissa] Before the
race, Lucas gets serious

00:01:50.778 --> 00:01:52.252
and he gets his race face on

00:01:52.252 --> 00:01:53.649
and they're ready to compete.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:55.744
[Crowd] Two, one!

00:01:55.744 --> 00:01:57.635
(crowd cheering)

00:01:57.635 --> 00:02:01.575
- [Alissa] They swim around 200 yards.

00:02:01.575 --> 00:02:04.158
Then they transition to a bike.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:09.203
They'll go usually about
three to five miles.

00:02:09.203 --> 00:02:12.326
- [Brian] And then
they'll run about a mile.

00:02:12.326 --> 00:02:15.054
Noah's strong physically
and especially mentally.

00:02:15.054 --> 00:02:16.587
Because he's truly only doing these races

00:02:16.587 --> 00:02:17.920
for his brother.

00:02:18.957 --> 00:02:20.606
- [Noah] Sometimes I feel like, God,

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:23.875
it's gotta be over soon, right?

00:02:23.875 --> 00:02:25.638
But I just hear Lucas.

00:02:25.638 --> 00:02:27.257
- [Lucas] (vocalizing)

00:02:27.257 --> 00:02:29.859
- [Noah] That's how he says, “Go faster".

00:02:29.859 --> 00:02:30.756
- [Kid] Come on, go go go!

00:02:30.756 --> 00:02:32.366
- [Woman] Go, buddy, go go go! Nice!

00:02:32.366 --> 00:02:33.592
(cowbell ringing)

00:02:33.592 --> 00:02:36.235
- Every day is precious
with that little boy.

00:02:36.235 --> 00:02:38.268
I try to soak in the experience,

00:02:38.268 --> 00:02:40.608
because we don't know how long the boys

00:02:40.608 --> 00:02:43.009
will be able to do triathlons together.

00:02:43.009 --> 00:02:45.270
Any one of them could be their last.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:46.861
What these boys accomplish gives me

00:02:46.861 --> 00:02:48.997
an immense sense of pride.

00:02:48.997 --> 00:02:51.184
- Noah and Lucas are an inspiration.

00:02:51.184 --> 00:02:53.510
People see these two young boys,

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:56.726
and it gives them hope and
it gives them encouragement

00:02:56.726 --> 00:02:59.893
to go out and tackle life challenges.

